wg-shield-stats-title = Generator stats
wg-shield-stats-generator = Generator: { $name }
wg-shield-stats-capacity = Heat capacity: { $value } (limited by power or overload)
wg-shield-stats-overload-limit = Overload threshold: { $value } heat
wg-shield-stats-online-repair = Cooling, field raised: { $value } heat/s
wg-shield-stats-offline-repair = Cooling, recharge mode: { $value } heat/s
wg-shield-stats-idle-power = Idle power: { $value } kW
wg-shield-stats-max-power = Configured maximum power: { $value } kW
wg-shield-stats-overload-lockout = Overload lockout: { $value } seconds after heat falls below the threshold.
wg-shield-stats-recovery-note = Damage the field absorbs becomes heat, point for point, and power demand rises with heat. Actual recovery also depends on heat, power and recharge. The shield panel shows the current recovery estimate.
wg-shield-stats-costs = Raised field: -{ $thrust }% thrust, -{ $turn }% turning, hotter on long-range sensors. Overrun by heat, it collapses and locks ship guns for { $seconds } seconds.
wg-shield-stats-no-costs = Raised field: no cost to thrust, turning or guns.
wg-shield-stats-vent = Cooling, field down: { $value } heat/s
wg-shield-stats-fire-heat = Firing through the raised field: { $percent }% of each shot's damage comes back as heat. Guns hold fire at { $hold }% heat until the ship cools to { $resume }%.
wg-shield-stats-no-fire-heat = Firing through the raised field adds no heat.
